From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sid Manning <atx0x200@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:25:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mountd: fix mountstat3 pointer type mismatch for MNT1

get_rootfh() always takes a 'mountstat3 *' for its error output
argument, but the v2 mount protocol's fhstatus.fhs_status field is
declared 'u_int' (its own XDR routine passes it to xdr_u_int()),
while the v3 mountres3.fhs_status field is declared 'mountstat3'.
mount_mnt_1_svc() (the v2 MNT handler) passed &res->fhs_status
straight through, an incompatible pointer type that GCC only warns
about but Clang treats as an error by default.

Both fields are 4-byte integers occupying the same value domain
(get_rootfh() only ever stores MNT3ERR_* values, which fit the v2
status field just as they always have), so a local cast at this one
call site is sufficient. Changing fhstatus.fhs_status's declared
type instead would only move the same error to its xdr_u_int() call
in mount_xdr.c.

Signed-off-by: Sid Manning <atx0x200@gmail.com>
---
 utils/mountd/mountd.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/utils/mountd/mountd.c b/utils/mountd/mountd.c
index 3eda7d343..0bcd9552d 100644
--- a/utils/mountd/mountd.c
+++ b/utils/mountd/mountd.c
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@
 	xlog(D_CALL, "Received MNT1(%s) request from %s", *path,
 		host_ntop(sap, buf, sizeof(buf)));
 
-	fh = get_rootfh(rqstp, path, NULL, &res->fhs_status, 0);
+	fh = get_rootfh(rqstp, path, NULL, (mountstat3 *)&res->fhs_status, 0);
 	if (fh)
 		memcpy(&res->fhstatus_u.fhs_fhandle, fh->fh_handle, 32);
 	return 1;
--
2.46.2
